<script src="/js/easy.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/menu.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/form.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/inplace.js?version=545"></script><script>EC.version='545'</script></head>
<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="single"><div id="cfptitle">IEEE LatinIoT 2027: IEEE Latin American Conference on Internet of Things</div><div id="cfpvenue">ICON Hotel Santiago</div><div id="cfpdateplace">Santiago, Chile, April 28-30, 2027</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=ieeelatiniot2027" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=ieeelatiniot2027</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>November 28, 2026</td></tr></table><div class="topics">Topics: <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=254476" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_carmin bg_yellow">internet of things (iot)</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=154661" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_bluelight bg_aqua">cyber physical systems</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=840" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_black bg_seagreenlight">embedded systems</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=18792020" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_bluelight bg_powderblue">wireless communications and networking</span></a></div><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Call for Papers </strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>IEEE LatinIoT 2027 - April 28-30, 2027 | Santiago, Chile</strong></p><p>The<strong> 2nd</strong> <strong>IEEE Latin American Conference on Internet of Things (IEEE LatinIoT 2027)</strong> will be held in Santiago, Chile, from <u>April 28 to 30, 2027</u>. LatinIoT is an international flagship conference of the IEEE Internet of Things Technical Community, providing a multidisciplinary forum for researchers, practitioners, industry professionals, and students from Latin America and around the world to exchange ideas, experiences, and advances across the broad field of the Internet of Things (IoT). LatinIoT 2027 seeks original contributions addressing the theoretical and technological foundations of IoT, communications and networking, sensing and embedded systems, computing and intelligence, security and privacy, emerging applications, experimentation, and real-world deployments.</p><p>The 2027 edition will place particular emphasis on <em>"Networking and IoT technologies enabling human-centered and industrial cyber-physical systems"</em>, highlighting the integration of sensing, communication, computation, control, and intelligence across physical and digital environments. The conference will foster international collaboration and knowledge exchange around emerging technologies and applications shaping the evolution of IoT and cyber-physical systems.</p><h2>Submission Guidelines</h2><p>All papers must be original and not simultaneously submitted to another journal or conference. The following paper categories are welcome.</p><ul><li><strong>Full papers (up to 6 pages)</strong> presenting mature and complete research results with substantial technical contributions.</li><li><strong>Short papers (up to 4 pages)</strong> presenting focused contributions, preliminary results, work in progress, or proof-of-concept studies.</li></ul><p>Papers must be written in English using the IEEE conference format (10-point font, double-column, single-space). Both short papers of up to four (4) pages and full papers of up to six (6) pages, including figures and references, will be accepted.</p><h2>List of Topics</h2><p>Relevant technical topics include, but are not limited to:</p><ul><li>IoT Communications, Networking, 6G</li><li>Antennas, Propagation, Measurements, and Testbeds for IoT</li><li>Circuits, Electronics, Embedded Systems, and Design Automation</li><li>Sensors, Sensing, and Signal Processing for IoT and CPS</li><li>AI, Machine Learning, Edge Intelligence, and Data Analytics</li><li>Control, Robotics, and Autonomous Cyber-Physical Systems</li><li>Reliability, Trustworthiness, Cybersecurity, Privacy, and Resilience</li><li>Human-Centered CPS, eHealth, and Assistive Technologies</li><li>Industrial CPS, Critical IoT, and Digital Twins</li><li>IoT and CPS for Energy, Transportation, and Smart Infrastructure</li><li>IoT Architectures, Interoperability, Standards, and Emerging Technologies</li></ul><h2>Organizing Committee</h2><h3>General Chairs</h3><ul><li>Miguel Gutiérrez Gaitán, PUC, Chile</li><li>Samuel Montejo-Sánchez, UTEM, Chile</li></ul><h3>Technical Program Committee Chairs</h3><ul><li>Felipe Núñez, PUC, Chile</li><li>Oana Iova, INSA Lyon, France</li></ul><h3>Publicity Chairs</h3><ul><li>Yéssica Sáez, UTP, Panama</li><li>Juan A. Fraire, INRIA Lyon, France</li><li>Marco Martaló, U. Cagliari, Italy</li></ul><h3>Keynote Speaker Chairs</h3><ul><li>Mauricio Rodríguez, PUCV, Chile</li><li>Carlos A. Gutiérrez, UASLP, México</li></ul><h3>Tutorial Chairs</h3><ul><li>Carlos Lozano, U. Andes, Colombia</li><li>Silvia E. Restrepo, UCSC, Chile</li></ul><h3>Publication Chairs</h3><ul><li>Ricardo Reis, UFRGS, Brazil</li><li>Victor Grimblatt, Synopsys, Chile</li></ul><h3>IEEE IoT-TC Advising Committee</h3><ul><li>Ricardo Reis, UFRGS, Brazil</li><li>Victor Grimblatt, Synopsys, Chile</li></ul><p> </p><h2>Keynote Speakers &amp; Panelists</h2><ul><li>Ana García Armada, UC3M, Spain</li><li>Onel L. Alcaráz López, U. Oulu, Finland</li></ul><p>Other speakers to be announced soon.</p><h2>Publication</h2><p>All accepted papers presented in person at the conference will be submitted for inclusion in the IEEE Xplore Digital Library. </p><h2>Venue</h2><p>The conference will be held at the ICON Hotel Santiago. </p><h2>Contact</h2><p>All questions about submissions should be emailed to <strong>miguel.gutierrez@uc.cl</strong></p><h2>Sponsors</h2><p>The IEEE LatinIoT conference is an official IEEE conference sponsored by the IEEE IoT Technical Community. The 2027 conference will be co-sponsored by IEEE ComSoc Chile and the Cyber-Physical Systems Research and Technology Center (CPS-RTC). </p></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
